Plasma physics (@plasma-physics: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_0S8HNABDKT1SVXEGYD76B04ERN
Plasma physics studies collective behaviour in matter containing mobile charged particles. The material covers particle motion, electromagnetic coupling, waves, instabilities, transport, confinement, and high-energy-density conditions, connecting laboratory plasmas, fusion research, industrial processing, and naturally occurring space plasmas.

**Common preparation developed:** the [uniform-field motion lesson](../core/Derive-uniform-magnetic-motion-without-assigning-work-to-deflection.lingua) derives signed nonrelativistic motion, center and conserved kinetic energy under a prescribed external field. Its exact investigation distinguishes deflection from work; collective behavior, self-consistent fields, collisions, instabilities and full plasma formation remain pending.

**Parent:** [Physics — fields, matter, motion and physical evidence](../Physics.lingua#r_04A5CP8RTBERZEN4XCCDQ3T47W).
